{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A] I never meant to cause you any [F#m7]sorrow,
[E] I never meant to cause you any [Dsus2]pain.
[A] I only wanted one time t[F#m7]o see you laughing,
I [E7]only want to see you laughing i[Dsus2]n the purple [A]rain.
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
Purple rain, Purple [Dsus2]rain.
Purple rain, Purple [A]rain.
[F#m7] Purple rain, Purple [E]rain.  [E]
I [E7]only want to see you bathing i[Dsus2]n the purple [A]rain.
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I never wanted to be your weekend lover no[A], no.   [F#m7]
[E] I only wanted to be some kind of [Dsus2]friend.
[A] Baby I could never steal you from [F#m7]another,
It's such a [E7]shame, it's such a shame our [Dsus2]friendship had to [A]end.
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
Purple rain, Purple [Dsus2]rain.
Purple rain, Purple [A]rain.
[F#m7]Purple rain, Purple [E]rain.  [E]
I [E7]only want to see you bathing i[Dsus2]n the purple [A]rain.
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Honey I know, I know, I know times are [A]changing... [F#m7]
It's time, it's [E]time, it's time we all reach out for something [Dsus2]new - me, you.
[A] You say you want a leader, but [F#m7]you can't seem to make up your mind.
Baby you better close [E7]it - and let me g[Dsus2]uide you to the purple [A]rain.
{end_of_verse}


